[center][size=6][b]DAORework[/b][/size]
[size=4]A free mod manager, launcher and diagnostics tool for Dragon Age: Origins[/size][/center]

[img]https://daorework.dilly-world.net/images/00-cover.png[/img]

Already have mods installed by hand? DAORework takes them over [b]without reinstalling anything[/b], and from then on every change shows you exactly what it will do first, takes a backup, and can be rolled back.

[line]

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Adopts the mods you installed by hand[/b] in [i]override[/i] and [i]AddIns[/i], without reinstalling them. Official DLC is never touched.
[*][b]Installs mods safely.[/b] Import a .dazip, .zip, .7z or .rar, or drop it on the window. Activating shows exactly what will be copied, replaced or removed before anything changes, takes a backup first, and any change can be rolled back.
[*][b]Shows conflicts.[/b] For every file two mods share, it shows whose copy the game uses, and lets you reorder them.
[*][b]Checks every mod.[/b] Programs inside a mod are named and never installed. Every mod is scanned by your own antivirus (Microsoft Defender or whichever you use) before it is kept, and a mod it flags is refused. A download that differs from the known official one is pointed out.
[*][b]Fixes.[/b] Installs and removes DXVK, and the 4 GB (large address aware) patch on copies that allow it, and notices when Steam's Verify integrity has undone a fix. The 4 GB patch is for copies without Steam's copy protection, such as GOG and EA App: Steam refuses to start its own daorigins.exe once it is patched, so DAORework does not patch the Steam copy, and tells you how to undo it if it was patched before.
[*][b]Diagnoses your install[/b] and suggests next steps, each with its own button.
[*][b]Backs up your saves[/b], keeping the newest backups, and launches the game.
[/list]

[b]What it does not do:[/b] it does not include or download any game files or mods, and it never sends anything over the internet. It only changes the game's own files for the two fixes, each behind a plan and a backup.

